    "['remote-ip [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'neighbor 3.3.3.9 remote-as [AS-number]', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]', 'mpls ldp autoconfig'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nneighbor 3.3.3.9 remote-as [AS-number]\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Cisco's MPLS LDP implementation, you would typically specify the neighbor under `mpls ldp` configuration mode. However, the exact equivalent depends on the context:\\n1. For basic LDP neighbor configuration, the above command is used (though it requires an AS number)\\n2. If this is for L2VPN signaling, Cisco uses `xconnect` or `l2vpn` commands with target address\\n\\nThe most direct functional equivalent in Cisco for establishing an LDP session would be:\\n##\\nmpls ldp neighbor 3.3.3.9 targeted\\n##\\n\\nChoose based on your specific implementation needs. The first is BGP-style neighbor configuration, while the second is Cisco's native MPLS LDP neighbor command.\", 'trans_template': 'neighbor 3.3.3.9 remote-as [AS-number]'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'mpls ldp neighbor 3.3.3.9 targeted', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]', 'mpls ldp autoconfig'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nneighbor 3.3.3.9 remote-as [AS-number]\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Cisco's MPLS LDP implementation, you would typically specify the neighbor under `mpls ldp` configuration mode. However, the exact equivalent depends on the context:\\n1. For basic LDP neighbor configuration, the above command is used (though it requires an AS number)\\n2. If this is for L2VPN signaling, Cisco uses `xconnect` or `l2vpn` commands with target address\\n\\nThe most direct functional equivalent in Cisco for establishing an LDP session would be:\\n##\\nmpls ldp neighbor 3.3.3.9 targeted\\n##\\n\\nChoose based on your specific implementation needs. The first is BGP-style neighbor configuration, while the second is Cisco's native MPLS LDP neighbor command.\", 'trans_template': 'mpls ldp neighbor 3.3.3.9 targeted'}]]": 1,
